{
  "_note": "ALL NUMBERS PLACEHOLDER — straight from pressure-model-illumination.md §4.3, which flags them as guesses. This is the Illumination pattern worked in full; the other seven targets are added by extending this file, not by touching code. A source names its own contributions, and every contribution beyond the one you bind is an IMPLICIT SECONDARY that happens whether you asked for it or not — 'you cannot have bright without hot unless you do something about it'. 'character' is per-target and decides HOW a source contributes: illumination's cyclic sources lift only the peak, constant ones lift peak and floor, occluding ones push both down. 'attachesTo' is the ONE target a source may be bound to. The rune spec §5 says 'each attaches to a target' but never says which — so these follow the spec's own grouping (Celestial, Water, Fire & Thermal, Stone & Mineral, Air, Living, Strange), because a thing attaches to the target it IS an instance of, not to whichever dial it happens to move furthest. Rain can't illuminate. Everything a source does beyond its target still happens as an implicit secondary — you just can't WRITE it. PLACEHOLDER; the palette and the grammar both follow this field. 'attachesTo' is a LIST of the targets a source may be bound to — everything else it does still happens as an implicit secondary. It is a list because some causes belong to more than one target: a volcano is heat and a mountain, a glacier is water and a valley. PLACEHOLDER: Relief currently borrows six sources this way and has no words of its own (volcano, glacier, granite, rift, sand, canopy). Whether it should get its own source runes — mountain, canyon, plain, dune, terrace — is Aimee's call, not mine to invent.",
